              <section class="av_textblock_section " itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/CreativeWork">
                <div class='avia_textblock  ' itemprop="text">
                  <p><strong>If you&#8217;re wondering how to get a drywall quantity takeoff, here are a few steps to take:</strong></p>
                  <p><strong>Measure Out:</strong> The 1st step in any estimate is to take a precise and detailed evaluation of the entire place that will be drywalled.</p>
                  <p><strong>Drywall Sheets:</strong> After that, we&#8217;ll figure out how many plates of drywall you&#8217;ll need to finish the job. We&#8217;ll also factor in a percentage for waste and errors to make sure that you do have sufficient material to finish the job not too much.</p>
                  <p><strong>Joint hybrid:</strong> Once you&#8217;ve sheeted and taped, you&#8217;ll need to figure out how much Joint hybrid you&#8217;ll need.</p>
                  <p><strong>Drywall Screws:</strong> Sometimes it&#8217;s the little factors that bring up. We&#8217;ll estimate how many screws you&#8217;ll need to complete the entire project.</p>
                  <p><strong>Square Beads:</strong> All through the project, we&#8217;ll measure the corners and provide the appropriate number of corner beads for all of your inner or outer corners.</p>
                  <p><strong>Labor Costs:</strong> Depending on the size of your construction process, the speed of construction companies, and 8 hour and project-based rates, we can calculate labour costs.</p>
                  <p><strong>Miscellaneous Accessories:</strong> All effects, sandpaper, service charges, authorization, site repair work, and cleanup will be considered.</p>
